---
import { Mascot } from "~/components/Mascot";
import { countries } from "~/data";
import { SITE } from "~/data/site";
import { aboutAlternates } from "~/i18n/routes";
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { shellAlternates } from "~/lib/hreflang";
---

<Base
  title="How leavemaxxing plans your leave"
  description="How leavemaxxing finds the leave days that turn weekends and public holidays into the longest breaks, and where the holiday data comes from."
  hreflangs={shellAlternates(aboutAlternates(SITE.url))}
>
  <article class="card mx-auto mt-2 max-w-3xl p-6 sm:p-10">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
      <Mascot size={64} mood="wow" title="" />
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold sm:text-4xl">How leavemaxxing plans your leave</h1>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-lm mt-6">
      <p>
        Most of your time off is already in the calendar: weekends and public holidays. leavemaxxing finds the few
        workdays that join them into long breaks, so each leave day you spend buys as many days away as possible.
      </p>

      <h2>What happens when you plan</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>We load the public holidays for your country, and your region if you pick one.</li>
        <li>
          Every day of your leave year is marked as a day off (weekend, holiday, or a day off you added) or a workday you
          could take.
        </li>
        <li>
          The planner checks every way of spending your leave days and keeps the best one. It doesn't guess or take
          shortcuts: for the style you choose, the plan it shows is the best possible one.
        </li>
        <li>
          It keeps your plan spread across the year, so you don't end up with every break in spring and nothing after
          summer.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>The three styles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Long weekends</strong> favours lots of 3 to 5 day breaks. It usually gives the highest score.</li>
        <li><strong>Balanced</strong> aims for week-long breaks while still using holidays well.</li>
        <li><strong>One big trip</strong> piles your leave into as long a break as it can.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can also set the shortest and longest break you want, favourite months, the days you work, and when your leave
        year starts. Tap any day in the calendar to keep it as leave, block it, or mark it as a day off.
      </p>

      <h2>Where the holidays come from</h2>
      <p>
        Holidays for {countries.length} countries and their regions come from the open source
        <a href="https://github.com/commenthol/date-holidays">date-holidays</a> project, licensed
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/">CC BY 3.0</a>. The site is rebuilt every week to pick up
        changes. Governments sometimes add or move holidays at short notice, so always check the dates with your employer
        before booking anything.
      </p>

      <h2>Your plans stay with you</h2>
      <p>
        There are no accounts. Plans are worked out in your browser, saved plans stay on your device, and a shared link
        carries the whole plan in the address itself. Read the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for details.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
